  "worked_solution": "The power set of $X,$ denoted $P(X),$ is the set that contains every possible subset of $X,$ including the empty set $\u2205.$\n\nSo, let's list all possible subsets of $X$ using a tree diagram. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14098182/assets/580d7c32378a2af641fb1066cec4ec24cc6c5b140ccf9475f9a3e3a68367d30d.png)\n\nAccording to our diagram, the subsets of $X$ are\n\n$$\n\u2205={},\\,{2},\\,{4},\\,{8},\\,{2,4},\\,{2,8},\\,{4,8},\\,{2,4,8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(X)={\u2205,{2},{4},{8},{2,4},{2,8},{4,8},{2,4,8}}.\n$$",
